<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Akyem Abuakwa</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1874 CE (approx.) · capital Kyebi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Akan kingdom of the eastern Gold Coast forest, rich in gold and later a stronghold of the cocoa economy, ruled by the Okyenhene from Kyebi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Akyem peoples moved into the forest of the Birim valley by the 16th century, and Akyem Abuakwa became the largest of their states. It lay across the routes from the coast to the interior, near rich gold deposits.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Okyenhene ruled with divisional chiefs, queen mothers and the councils typical of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> states. Akyem Abuakwa mined gold and traded it to the coast. In 1730 it joined with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-akyem-kotoku">Akyem Kotoku</a> and the Ga to overthrow <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/akwamu">Akwamu</a>. It then fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> for decades, sometimes as its tributary and sometimes as a rebel.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Akyem Abuakwa allied with the British against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> and came under British rule with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gold-coast-colony">Gold Coast Colony</a> in 1874. In the 20th century it became a heartland of cocoa farming, and the Okyenhene still reigns at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyebi">Kyebi</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1874 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.44%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1874 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kyebi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ofori Panin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Akan religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Twi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ghana">Ghana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Akyem, Akim, Akyem Abuakwa kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1687&amp;focus=akyem-abuakwa" aria-label="Akyem Abuakwa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4635 1941 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Akyem Abuakwa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4955 2197L4973 2230M4955 2197L4995 2226"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4973 2230h0M4995 2226h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4955 2197h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4955 2197h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kyebi. <a href="/atlas?year=1687&amp;focus=akyem-abuakwa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

